      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## MiniMax H3 - TURBO + REF2VA (multi-character) - R9700\n\nLocks character appearance to **reference images** instead of prompt wording.\nUp to **9** reference images, 3 reference videos, 3 reference audios.\n\n**Verified: the 4-step Turbo LoRA works on the ref2va checkpoint.**\nAll 259 LoRA modules exist in ref2va and the two checkpoints have identical\nmodule sets. Measured ~50 s for a 5.2 s clip at 640x352, everything cached.\n\n### How to use references\n- `ref_image_0` is wired to the hero (**gator_hero_ref.png**) and is ACTIVE.\n- `ref_image_1` is wired to a second character but ships **MUTED** - select it\n  and press **Ctrl+M** to enable, then pick your villain PNG.\n- `ref_image_2` is an empty slot; drag a LoadImage into it for a third.\n\nIn the prompt, refer to them **in slot order** as `<Picture 1>`, `<Picture 2>`,\n`<Picture 3>`. Slot `ref_image_0` = `<Picture 1>`.\n\nPut reference PNGs in ComfyUI's `input` folder. Grab one from an existing clip:\n`python extract_last_frame.py myclip.mp4 --name villain_ref`\n\n### Keep ref_image_size on \"match\"\n`max` uses a 2048 short edge and the node's own tooltip warns it \"can be several\ntimes slower\" - reference tokens ride through EVERY sampling step.\n\n### Same hard rules as the fl2va turbo workflow\n- **STEPS = 4.** Step-distilled schedule `[1.0, 0.973, 0.9231, 0.8, 0.0]`.\n  8 steps is WORSE, not better.\n- **Turbo Sampler required** - a plain KSamplerSelect will not work.\n- **strength 0.70** here; raise toward 0.85-1.0 for more sharpness/grain.\n\n### Speed\nEach reference image adds tokens that persist through every step, so refs cost\nroughly like extra resolution. 640x352 / 124f with one ref ~ 50 s.\n\nFirst render after any change pays one-time costs:\nnew prompt ~65 s encode, new canvas ~25 s-3 min autotune (cached forever),\nnew checkpoint ~50 s disk load. Iterating **seed** or **strength** is ~50 s.\n\n### Launch\n`Launch ComfyUI AMD RDNA4.bat`\n"
      ]
    },
